**Version**: 0.2
**Created**: 2026-07-07
**Status**: Pass 2 OPERATIONAL (2026-07-07). Python reference interpreter `render/engine/dsl.py` (tokenizer → recursive-descent parser → own-AST tree-walking evaluator, zero `eval`/`exec`/`compile`/`__import__`); conformance corpus `render/engine/dsl_conformance/dsl_corpus.json` (**226 cases, IEEE-754-bit-exact matching**, format `composeux-dsl-conformance-v1`, language-agnostic + README — the byte-contract for Pass 2b/JS) with reference adapter + runner; `expr:` promoted from refused → sanctioned at the three sites; the jump-drive triad re-authored to `expr:` (single-expression readiness AND, real variable-rate drain, `min()` conditional pump rate) — **[CXC-HW] C2 CLOSED**. Sandbox proven: malicious exprs (`__import__`, attribute/subscript access, unknown calls) fail at PARSE. CXC-DSL-C1…C12 all PASS; 570 tests green macOS (325 baseline + 245 DSL incl. the 226 corpus cases now CI-enforced, `tests/render/test_dsl.py`). **Pass 2b = C++/CYD interpreter, JS = Web tier — each its own pass, gated ONLY on passing this corpus byte-for-byte.** round() pinned half-to-even; float64 everywhere; guarded div/mod → 0.0; no transcendentals in v1.

**Pass 2b OPERATIONAL (2026-07-09) — define-once PROVEN on silicon.** C++/CYD interpreter `cyd/src/dsl.{h,cpp}` (host-compilable, `double` everywhere, own-AST recursive-descent, bounded recursion for the MCU); corpus→C++ header generator `python/scripts/gen_dsl_corpus_header.py` → `cyd/test/dsl_corpus_generated.h` (cases baked into flash, no JSON parser / no FS on the MCU); native host harness (`[env:native_dsl]`, the hardware-free CI foothold) + on-device runner (`[env:cyd_dsl_test]`). Results: native **234/234**, **on-device 226/226 on the real ESP32 xtensa soft-double** (device `(a device id, not published)`, 254 µs/case), Python reference **234/234** — expression eval now bit-identical across macOS arm64 / x86_64 / ESP32. Plus a 30k-expression differential fuzz vs the reference = 0 mismatches. **Falsification payoff:** 2b (the first independent implementation) exposed a latent reference non-totality (see [CXC-DSL-SEMANTICS] change record) — fixed, corpus 226→234. JS/Web-tier interpreter still owed, gated on this same corpus.
